answer:
According to Article 234(3) of the Constitution of Kenya, the following offices in the public service are explicitly excluded from the general applicability of clauses (1) and (2):

a. State offices;
b. an office of high commissioner, ambassador, or other diplomatic or consular representative of the Republic;
c. an office or position subject to:
   i. the Parliamentary Service Commission;
   ii. the Judicial Service Commission;
   iii. the Teachers Service Commission;
   iv. the National Police Service Commission;
d. an office in the service of a county government, except as contemplated in clause (2)(i).

These exclusions are detailed in the High Court judgment from [chunk_id: Law Society of Kenya v Attorney General (Sued on Behalf of the President of Kenya)  6 others Katiba Institute (Interested Party) (Petition E273of2024) 2025KEHC15858(KLR) (Constitutional and Human Rights) (7November2025) (Judgment)__s7__c7].
